From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Topher Campbell <chrs2021@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH 13/16] ASoC: mediatek: mt8183: Titan Pocket audio; codecs: add FS1860, MT6358 accdet

The MT6771's AFE is the MT8183's; this adds the Titan Pocket machine
driver, the FS1860 speaker amplifier, the AFE's hardware gain and the
FM paths (hostless and through the CPU), the modem's voice links
(Hostless_Speech, PCM 2; UL2 and I2S3 from the modem's downlink), the PCM
DAIs' own rate codes (the general ones left PCM 2 at 8 kHz), and jack
detection: an MT6358 ACCDET driver and the card's headset jack. The
MT6358 codec keeps the handset gain across its power-down (it came back
at -40 dB) and starts it at -10 dB; the AFE writes a stream's buffer
address again on every prepare, as deep sleep loses that register.
